  "contracts": [
    "Locate full current/old ActorCommand, ActorRouteSteps and old mixed ActorRoutePixels algorithms before translation. Do not adopt the ActorLaborer/Civic wrappers. Reuse complete ordinary C and true canonical children, never original IL or placeholder callbacks.",
    "4B7B50 existing C had correct morale logic in a rearranged logical state. Factor that algorithm once into formation_morale_apply; retain old logical API as support without second Native credit. New owner reads actual BCB9C8+id*144 record: kindWORD04, leaderWORD48, enemy subtypeBYTE6A, moraleWORD2C. WORD addition wraps then max/zero clamp; intermediate publication retained. Existing field names remain aliases; no independent synthesized formation table.",
    "4B7AB0 recalculates actual figures before fresh member BYTE28. Numerator1 and BYTE0..255 denominator prove4CDE60 cannot overflow; zero denominator retains actual0. Exact percentage thresholds8/10/14/20/30 and penalties-5/-7/-10/-12/-15/-20 call actual-layout morale provider.",
    "4BC4A0 preserves both cached formation WORD60 inputs before early exits. Actual ownerBYTE vs full playerDWORD; model category/limit/attack/defense DWORDs with stride56. Actor counterDWORD134 gates wrapped power*4; wrapped signed(30-defense)/20 then wrapped product is clamped only if negative. Accumulated damage wrapsBYTE1D; signed model maximum comparison, actual lowBYTE classifiers, formation strengthWORD7A saturation100, death action/wait stores and real cue/loss/combat sound branches retained.",
    "4B5050 exact13 target DWORDs and92 remap bytes at5174/51A8 match old cue C, including all nineteen explicit kinds and remaining random default. Use actual canonical rand seed/state; variant3. Shifted sample division32768 remains signed. No random or audio stand-in.",
    "4B1210 and4B1700 have separately authenticated77-byte remaps with seven exclusions25/77/78/92/93/100/101. Keep actual class/state/type reloads, special resource/arrest/temple interactions, bounded chain999 transitions and eight actual neighbor DWORDs with signedWORD heads. Profile view atEA5C88 has exact49D8 stride; counterDWORD00, gateWORD60, buildingDWORD314, with unresolved semantics retaining address labels.",
    "Contact pair keeps old coordinate WORD18/1A versus target position/destination WORD14/16 and24/26 branches, cached/fresh reads, action-before-combat BYTE10, directionBYTE11, queueBYTE8B and WORD8C/8E/90. Delay is BYTE6A in reserved_06a, not leading WORD68. Offset assertions compile in canonical and worktree; all existing storage names/size preserved.",
    "4B3FF0 detaches before even a nonpositive-step run and reattaches afterward. BYTE1C decrements before signed delta gate; real three motion leaves, full EAX0/1. X WORD14 store precedes fresh pixelY4C read; base DWORD is loaded before Y WORD16 store; fresh X forms wrapped base+x+228*y. Native terrain test is BYTE at a DWORD pool unit, and timerBYTE40 update is preserved.",
    "4B3C60 captures old coordinates before unlink. Signed direction>=8 returns before unlink, whereas negative signed direction reaches unsigned>7 return after unlink. Exact8-direction table and6 bridge targets match live Ghidra; bridge heights0/15/27/14/30/36 and all six ship exclusions retained. WORD coordinates/DWORD tile wrap; actual terrain/bridge/chain children; old coordinates publish after contact. Query records beginBCD5F8, movement viewsBCD600: Native height6F/71 in the latter is query77/79. Do not cast the two views at the same base.",
    "All8 public canonical owners have one compiled definition. Existing logical morale API remains compatible and shares the one C algorithm. Actual compiled canonical calls cover the entire child tree; compiler inlining of private helpers or parent tails gets no extra Native credit. Ghidra names/signatures/comments and complete pseudocode refreshed in the already-open original session."
  ],
